  "question": {
    "text": "Two persons pull a wire towards themselves. Each person exerts a force of $200 \\mathrm{~N}$ on the wire. Young's modulus of the material of wire is $1 \\times 10^{11} \\mathrm{~N} \\mathrm{~m}^{-2}$. Original length of the wire is $2 \\mathrm{~m}$ and the area of cross section is $2 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$. The wire will extend in length by ______ $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$200 \\mathrm{~N} \\longleftrightarrow O$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{\\mathrm{F}}{\\mathrm{A}}=\\mathrm{Y} \\frac{\\Delta \\ell}{\\ell} \\Rightarrow \\Delta \\ell=\\frac{\\mathrm{F} \\ell}{\\mathrm{AY}} \\\\ & \\Delta \\ell=\\frac{200 \\times 2}{2 \\times 10^{-4} \\times 10^{11}}=2 \\times 10^{-5}=20 \\mu \\mathrm{m}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
